{"born":[{"text":"f72b132dd1","mother":16,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":4,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":21,"rewritten":false},{"text":"d96a91250a","mother":15,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code improves survival by explicitly tracking harm vs. benefit per species, avoiding repeated ingestion of poisonous items, prioritizing eating when starved, and caching safe food in the pantry for later use to smooth out hunger spikes.","ms":7151},{"text":"23da0ccf0d","mother":6,"rewritten":false},{"text":"f35ceee18c","mother":3,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes survival by strictly avoiding fruits with any history of harm (h >= f), prevents redundant actions on safe foods by only eating/carriage based on hunger thresholds and carrying state, and uses 'taste' for novel fruits unless starvation is imminent (where the risk of death from poison outweighs the benefit of safe discovery, forcing a gamble on 'eat').","ms":12815},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":9,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":7,"rewritten":false},{"text":"23da0ccf0d","mother":6,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":19,"rewritten":false},{"text":"11a5e64abe","mother":3,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":5,"rewritten":false},{"text":"11a5e64abe","mother":3,"rewritten":false},{"text":"a51259d523","mother":6,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes known safe fruits for immediate consumption/carriage, avoids known harmful ones unless starving, and uses a higher hunger threshold for eating novel foods to reduce fatal mistakes, while distinguishing between \"safe\" (no harm recorded) and \"deadly\" (more harm than benefit) based on diary history.","ms":10635},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"9f411b51b3","mother":15,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code